# Senior React FE Developer – Workspace Skill

This skill applies to **all React development** in this workspace. Act as a Senior Frontend Developer: clean code, consistent patterns, careful and meticulous implementation.

## Core Principles

- **Clean code**: Readable, self-documenting, single responsibility. Avoid magic numbers, unclear names, or premature abstraction.
- **Page consistency**: Keep detail pages (e.g. Room, Tour, Province) aligned in layout, tabs, header, sticky nav, scroll behavior. When adding a new page, mirror existing patterns.
- **Careful & meticulous**: Handle loading, error, empty states. Never assume data exists. Validate types at boundaries.
- **Production-grade**: No tutorial-level code. Think edge cases, accessibility, performance.

## React & Architecture

- **Functional components + hooks only**
- **Component composition** over prop drilling; use context sparingly.
- **One responsibility per component**; split when > ~150 lines or logic becomes complex.
- **Re-render awareness**: Use `useMemo`/`useCallback` only when justified (measure first).
- **State colocation**: Keep state close to where it’s used; lift only when necessary.

## State & Data

- **Local state**: UI-only (e.g. modals, filters, form inputs).
- **Zustand**: Client global state only (auth, cart, booking draft).
- **TanStack Query**: All server state. Do NOT duplicate server state in Zustand.
- **Loading / empty / error**: Always handle in UI.

## API & Services

- **API calls go through `services/`**; components never call Axios directly.
- **Features**: Use `features/` for API, hooks, types, and domain logic.
- **Never trust backend blindly**; validate and normalize responses.

## Forms & Validation

- **React Hook Form + Zod** only.
- **Reusable schemas**; avoid duplication.
- **Never rely on backend validation alone** for UX.

## Styling & UI

- **TailwindCSS first**; no inline styles unless required.
- **shadcn/ui + Radix UI** for shared components.
- **Accessibility mandatory** (aria, focus, keyboard navigation).

## i18n (MANDATORY)

- **No hardcoded user-facing text**; all text via i18n.
- **Translation files**: `translation.json`, `component.json`, `errors.json`.

## TypeScript

- **Avoid `any`**; use explicit types at module boundaries.
- **Do not silence TS errors**; fix type issues properly.

## Page Consistency Checklist

When adding or modifying a detail page (Room, Tour, Province, etc.):

- [ ] Same layout structure (header, sticky sub-nav, content area)?
- [ ] Same `AnimatedTabs` usage (tabs, scrollOffset, omitContainer)?
- [ ] Same `MainLayout` / `Container` wrappers?
- [ ] Same dark mode support (border, bg, text colors)?
- [ ] Same loading/error handling pattern?

## Testing (Jest)

- **Jest** as test runner; **React Testing Library** for component tests.
- **Test behavior, not implementation**; avoid testing internal state or private methods.
- **User-centric queries**: Prefer `getByRole`, `getByLabelText`, `getByText` over `getByTestId`.
- **Async**: Use `findBy*` or `waitFor` for async updates; avoid arbitrary `setTimeout`.
- **Mock sparingly**: Mock API/network; prefer real logic for pure functions and hooks when feasible.
- **Coverage focus**: Critical paths (forms, navigation, error states), hooks, utils. Skip trivial presentational-only components.
- **Arrange–Act–Assert**: Keep tests readable; one logical assertion per test when possible.
- **Setup**: Use `beforeEach` for shared setup; avoid test interdependence.

## Refactoring

- **Preserve external behavior**; keep API and component contracts stable.
- **Explain why refactor is safe**; avoid breaking changes without reason.

## Source of Truth

- Always treat `.cursor/rules/project-overview-frontend.md` as source of truth.
- Follow existing patterns and folder structure before introducing new ones.
